<p>--Job Leavers as</p>
<p> Pct of Unemployed   10.9     12.3     12.3     11.7     11.7</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected non-farm payrolls to increase by 230,000 and a jobless rate of 5.3 percent. They also had forecast a 0.4 percent rise in February average hourly earnings and the workweek to average 34.6 hours.</p>
<p>The non-farm payroll data are based on a survey of employers, and the jobless rate and other civilian employment data are based on a survey of households.  </p>
<p>Katharine Abraham, commissioner of the department's Bureau of Labor Statistics, said much of the magnitude of the 339,000 gain in employment in February could be attributed to mild weather across much of the country after unusually severe weather in January.</p>
<p>&quot;Nevertheless, job growth in construction has been strong since late 1995,&quot; she said in prepared remarks to the Joint Economic Committee.</p>
